# docint — example configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` in the repository root. Both consumers read that same file:
# the backend through `load_dotenv()`, and Docker through `env_file` in
# docker/compose.yaml.
#
# This file covers what a deployment actually sets. The *complete* reference —
# every variable docint reads, with its default — is docs/configuration.md.
#
# Conventions used below:
#   - A commented line shows the real default. Uncomment only to change it.
#   - The few UNcommented lines are an opinionated starting point (the vllm
#     shape), not defaults — docint's own default provider is ollama.
#   - Booleans accept `true`, `1`, `yes` (case-insensitive) and nothing else.
#     `on`, `True ` with a trailing space, or a typo all read as FALSE, which
#     silently switches off a setting that defaults to true.
#   - `${OTHER_VAR}` is expanded by both consumers. Prefer plain literals here
#     unless you specifically want a host-shell override, and never write a
#     bare `${VAR}` without a `:-default` — on a clean host it resolves to an
#     empty string.


# =============================================================================
# 1. Required
# =============================================================================
# Supported providers: ollama | openai | vllm. An unknown value fails at
# startup rather than falling back.
INFERENCE_PROVIDER=vllm
OPENAI_API_BASE=http://vllm-router:4000/v1
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-no-key-required


# =============================================================================
# 2. Core
# =============================================================================
# Logging is one stderr sink; retention belongs to the compose logging driver.
# docs/ingestion.md § Observability explains how to read an ingest run.
# DOCINT_OFFLINE=1                    # 1 = load models from the local HF cache only (airgap default)
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO                      # stderr sink level: TRACE|DEBUG|INFO|WARNING|ERROR
# LOG_PROGRESS_INTERVAL_S=30          # heartbeat while one job stage repeats; 0 logs every message (thousands of lines on a large ingest)
# METRICS_ENABLED=true                # GET /metrics for the obs-plane scrape target
# RESPONSE_LANGUAGE=en                # en | de — switches prompts and UI strings; unknown falls back to en


# =============================================================================
# 3. Identity and access
# =============================================================================
# The edge gateway authenticates every request and injects the identity
# header. In production leave DOCINT_DEFAULT_IDENTITY UNSET so a request
# arriving without that header is rejected 401 — setting it makes the backend
# stop failing closed. The fallback is for local/single-user runs only.
# DOCINT_ADMIN_GROUP=admins           # group that may operate in another owner's namespace
# DOCINT_AUTH_HEADER=X-Auth-User      # trusted header carrying the principal
# DOCINT_DEFAULT_IDENTITY=            # unset in production; e.g. `operator` for local runs
# DOCINT_GROUPS_HEADER=X-Auth-Groups


# =============================================================================
# 4. Service endpoints
# =============================================================================
# BACKEND_PUBLIC_HOST does NOT inherit BACKEND_HOST — it falls back to the
# literal below, so setting only BACKEND_HOST in production leaves document
# preview links pointing at localhost.
# BACKEND_HOST=http://localhost:8000
# BACKEND_PUBLIC_HOST=http://localhost:8000
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
# QDRANT_HOST=http://localhost:6333
# SESSIONS_DB_PATH=~/docint/sessions.sqlite3   # consulted only when SESSION_STORE is unset
# SESSION_STORE=                      # full SQLAlchemy URL; wins outright when set
#
# Frontend build (Vite). Unset, the SPA derives its API base from BASE_URL,
# which is what the edge gateway's /docint/ sub-path deployment needs.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=


# =============================================================================
# 5. Models
# =============================================================================
# Defaults are per provider. Pick the block matching INFERENCE_PROVIDER above.
#
#   ollama:  EMBED_MODEL=bge-m3              TEXT_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b       VISION_MODEL=qwen3.5:9b
#   vllm:    EMBED_MODEL=BAAI/bge-m3         TEXT_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B   VISION_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B
#   openai:  EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small  TEXT_MODEL=gpt-4o        VISION_MODEL=gpt-4o
#
# EMBED_MODEL must be the Hugging Face repo id (BAAI/bge-m3) when pointing at
# the embed-only CPU container: it always serves bge-m3 and ignores the value,
# but the string is recorded as provenance in session metadata.
# EMBED_MODEL=BAAI/bge-m3
# EMBED_TOKENIZER_REPO=BAAI/bge-m3    # offline token counting; empty on openai
# NER_MODEL=gliner-community/gliner_large-v2.5
# RERANK_MODEL=BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3
# SPARSE_MODEL=BAAI/bge-m3            # same on every provider — sparse is always remote
# TEXT_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B
# TRANSLATE_MODEL=                    # inherits TEXT_MODEL
# VISION_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B        # captions images, and reads them when OCR_MODEL is unset


# =============================================================================
# 6. Per-lane inference endpoints
# =============================================================================
# Every lane defaults to the full vllm-service stack behind the LiteLLM router,
# so an unchanged stack needs none of these. Override a lane only when running
# its standalone CPU shape (`embed-only`, `rerank-only`, `clip-only`,
# `gliner-only`) beside a non-vllm chat provider.
#
# EMBED_* / SPARSE_* / RERANK_* / OCR_* inherit OPENAI_API_BASE and
# OPENAI_API_KEY. CLIP_* and NER_* do NOT — they default to the router alias
# below with no key, so on the full stack set their keys explicitly.
#
# TRAP: EMBED_API_BASE must include /v1 (the OpenAI SDK appends /embeddings to
# it), while SPARSE_API_BASE against the *same* container must not. One host,
# two forms — a missing /v1 surfaces as a 404 from the embedding endpoint.
#
# CLIP_API_BASE=http://vllm-router:4000
# CLIP_API_KEY=$OPENAI_API_KEY        # required on the router; leave unset for clip-only
# CLIP_TIMEOUT=30
# EMBED_API_BASE=                     # inherits OPENAI_API_BASE; embed-only: http://embed-only:8000/v1
# EMBED_API_KEY=                      # inherits OPENAI_API_KEY
# NER_API_BASE=http://vllm-router:4000   # gliner-only: http://gliner-only:8000
# NER_API_KEY=$OPENAI_API_KEY         # required on the router; leave unset for gliner-only
# NER_LABELS=                         # comma-separated; replaces the built-in entity set
# NER_THRESHOLD=0.3
# NER_TIMEOUT=30
# RERANK_API_BASE=                    # inherits OPENAI_API_BASE; rerank-only: http://rerank-only:8000
# RERANK_API_KEY=                     # inherits OPENAI_API_KEY
# RERANK_TIMEOUT=                     # inherits OPENAI_TIMEOUT
# SPARSE_API_BASE=                    # inherits OPENAI_API_BASE; embed-only: http://embed-only:8000
# SPARSE_API_KEY=                     # inherits OPENAI_API_KEY
# SPARSE_TIMEOUT=                     # inherits OPENAI_TIMEOUT
#
# Chat client itself:
# OPENAI_CTX_WINDOW=8192              # vllm: inherits CHAT_MAX_MODEL_LEN
# OPENAI_TIMEOUT=300


# =============================================================================
# 7. Document OCR
# =============================================================================
# One endpoint answers every "read this image": scanned PDF pages, table
# regions geometry could not recover, and image files.
#
# Leave OCR_MODEL unset and VISION_MODEL reads pages exactly as before, with
# image OCR off. A *layout* model (dots.mocr / dots.ocr) instead returns
# bounding boxes, categories and tables as HTML, so a scanned page chunks like
# a digital one. Anything else is asked for plain text.
# OCR_API_BASE=                       # inherits OPENAI_API_BASE
# OCR_API_KEY=                        # inherits OPENAI_API_KEY
# OCR_MODEL=                          # e.g. dots-studio/dots.mocr
# OCR_TIMEOUT=                        # inherits OPENAI_TIMEOUT; a page takes a minute or two
#
# PIPELINE_OCR_ENABLED=true
# PIPELINE_OCR_MAX_PIXELS=2007040     # 28*28*2560 — must NOT exceed the server's own cap
#                                     # (vllm-service OCR_MM_PROCESSOR_KWARGS), or the model
#                                     # resizes the render itself and answers in a frame the
#                                     # caller never saw. Below the cap is safe.
# PIPELINE_OCR_MAX_TOKENS=4096        # raise for a layout model: a page of JSON is long
# PIPELINE_TABLE_OCR=true             # re-read tables whose structure geometry could not recover
#
# Reading the text *inside* an image (screenshot, photographed letter, slide).
# Defaults to on wherever OCR_MODEL is set. Keyframes stay off until asked: a
# clip contributes many frames and only slides tend to carry text.
# IMAGE_OCR_ENABLED=                  # inherits: on iff OCR_MODEL is set
# KEYFRAME_OCR_ENABLED=false


# =============================================================================
# 8. PDF pipeline
# =============================================================================
# PIPELINE_ARTIFACTS_DIR=~/docint/artifacts
# PIPELINE_FORCE_REPROCESS=false      # ignore cached artifacts and re-run every stage
# PIPELINE_MAX_WORKERS=4
# PIPELINE_TEXT_COVERAGE_THRESHOLD=0.01   # chars-per-area below which a page counts as scanned


# =============================================================================
# 9. Ingestion and chunking
# =============================================================================
# COARSE_CHUNK_SIZE=8192              # parent chunk token budget
# DOCINT_INGEST_CONCURRENCY=1         # ingest jobs at once, process-wide; same collection is still refused (409)
# DOCSTORE_BATCH_SIZE=100
# FINE_CHUNK_SIZE=1024                # child chunk token budget
# INGESTION_BATCH_SIZE=50
# INGEST_BENCHMARK_ENABLED=false
# INGEST_FAIL_FAST=false
# INGEST_MANIFEST_ENABLED=true        # SQLite manifest; also caches Nextext transcripts by media hash
# STREAMING_READERS_ENABLED=true
#
# Audio/video extensions routed through the Nextext pre-pass (NOT the generic
# reader whitelist). Comma-separated; a leading dot is added if omitted.
# MEDIA_FILETYPES=.mp4,.mov,.mkv,.webm,.avi,.m4v,.mpg,.mpeg,.mp3,.m4a,.wav,.flac,.aac,.ogg,.opus,.wma


# =============================================================================
# 10. Embedding budget
# =============================================================================
# Out-of-range values here RAISE at startup rather than warning.
# EMBED_BATCH_SIZE=64                 # [1..1024]    ollama: 16 | vllm: 64 | openai: 100
# EMBED_CTX_TOKENS=8192               # [256..32768] ollama: 2048 | openai: 8191 | vllm: CHAT_MAX_MODEL_LEN
# EMBED_MAX_RETRIES=1                 # [0..10]      openai: 2
# EMBED_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600           # ollama: 1800 | vllm: 600 | openai: 60


# =============================================================================
# 11. Retrieval
# =============================================================================
# ENABLE_HYBRID is an explicit override. Left unset, hybrid is on when
# INFERENCE_PROVIDER=vllm or SPARSE_API_BASE is set explicitly, off otherwise —
# SPARSE_API_BASE alone cannot signal availability, since it inherits
# OPENAI_API_BASE silently.
# CHAT_RESPONSE_MODE=auto             # auto | compact | refine
# ENABLE_HYBRID=
# PARENT_CONTEXT_RETRIEVAL_ENABLED=true
# RETRIEVAL_HYBRID_ALPHA=0.5          # 0 = sparse only, 1 = dense only
# RETRIEVE_TOP_K=20
# SOCIAL_SOURCE_DIVERSITY_LIMIT=2     # max chunks per source document in one answer


# =============================================================================
# 12. Images as sources
# =============================================================================
# IMAGE_CACHE_BY_HASH=true            # skip re-embedding an image the companion already has
# IMAGE_INGESTION_ENABLED=true
# IMAGE_RERANK_MIN_SCORE=0.05         # reranker score an image must reach to surface as a source
# IMAGE_RETRIEVE_TOP_K=5              # CLIP candidates entering the ranking
# IMAGE_TAGGING_ENABLED=true          # caption + tags (a different task from OCR above)


# =============================================================================
# 13. Entities, NER and hate speech
# =============================================================================
# ENABLE_HATE_SPEECH_DETECTION=false
# HATE_SPEECH_MAX_WORKERS=1
# NER_ENABLED=true
# NER_MAX_CHARS=1024
# NER_MAX_WORKERS=4
#
# Entity resolution — the only way to merge semantically similar entities
# (USA / United States). Threshold and K raise at startup if out of range.
# RES_AUTO_RESOLVE=true               # run resolution as a stage inside the ingest job
# RES_EMBED_THRESHOLD=0.86            # [0..1] vector-match floor for one canonical entity
# RES_LLM_TIEBREAK=true               # conservative LLM adjudication of near-matches
# RES_VECTOR_K=5                      # [1..100] candidates fetched per surface form
#
# Analysis -> NER -> Graph. The SPA seeds its control from the first and lets
# the user raise it live up to the second.
# NER_GRAPH_MAX_TOP_K=500
# NER_GRAPH_TOP_K=80


# =============================================================================
# 14. Graph-assisted retrieval
# =============================================================================
# GRAPHRAG_ENABLED=true
# GRAPHRAG_MAX_NEIGHBORS=6
# GRAPHRAG_MIN_EDGE_WEIGHT=3
# GRAPHRAG_NEIGHBOR_HOPS=2
# GRAPHRAG_TOP_K_NODES=50


# =============================================================================
# 15. Nextext media processing (video / audio)
# =============================================================================
# docint ships no media runtime: each clip is forwarded to a remote Nextext
# service, which returns a transcript plus keyframes. Leave NEXTEXT_API_BASE
# unset to disable — video/audio is then skipped fail-soft, images unaffected.
#
# TRAP: NEXTEXT_API_BASE must include Nextext's /api/v1 prefix. docint calls
# {base}/jobs, so omitting it 404s every request.
#
# Nextext resolves the caller's identity from a trusted header and rejects
# header-less callers 401. docint sends NEXTEXT_IDENTITY under
# NEXTEXT_AUTH_HEADER on every request; set the identity empty to suppress the
# header and rely on Nextext's own default instead.
# NEXTEXT_API_BASE=                   # e.g. http://nextext-backend:8000/api/v1
# NEXTEXT_API_KEY=
# NEXTEXT_AUTH_HEADER=X-Auth-User     # must match Nextext's own
# NEXTEXT_IDENTITY=docint
# NEXTEXT_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4           # clips submitted in parallel per ingest
# NEXTEXT_POLL_INTERVAL=2
# NEXTEXT_POLL_MAX_SECONDS=1800       # wall-clock budget per job before status "timeout"
# NEXTEXT_TIMEOUT=30
#
# Keyframe sampling is configured HERE and forwarded as per-job options.
# docint always asks Nextext to sample (its extraction step is opt-in and
# defaults to off), so these rates are the off-switch: set either to 0 and no
# frames are produced.
# KEYFRAMES_MAX=20                    # hard ceiling per clip (Nextext rejects > 200)
# KEYFRAMES_PER_MINUTE=4
# KEYFRAME_DEDUP_COSINE=0.95          # [0..1] prune near-duplicate frames before storage
#
# Album linking. Some exports carry no media -> posting key at all (Telegram:
# Media ID == Network ID == the media's own message id), so a multi-item post
# leaves all but one media row naming no posting. Such rows attach to the first
# posting in their channel at or above their own message number, and ONLY when
# the timestamps agree within the tolerance below — that check is what keeps a
# partial export from silently attributing media to the wrong post. Exports that
# do carry a key never reach this path.
# SOCIAL_ALBUM_LINK_ENABLED=true
# SOCIAL_ALBUM_TOLERANCE_S=5          # seconds; widen only if a crawler stamps media late
#
# Timestamp linking. The last resort, tried only after both the manifest key and
# album inference have failed: a media row attaches to the single posting by the
# same author stamped at the same instant. Two postings at that instant, or none,
# leave the row unlinked rather than attached to a guess.
# SOCIAL_TIMESTAMP_LINK_ENABLED=true
#
# Text linking. The final fallback, for a shared post: the manifest records the
# original author while the export's own row is the sharer's, so no author-scoped
# rule can reach it. The row attaches to the single posting on its network whose
# text it repeats verbatim; two such postings, or none, leave it unlinked.
# SOCIAL_TEXT_LINK_ENABLED=true


# =============================================================================
# 16. Summaries and answer validation
# =============================================================================
# CORRECTIVE_RETRY_ENABLED=true       # re-answer once with a reformulated query when validation rejects
# RESPONSE_VALIDATION_ENABLED=true
# RESPONSE_VALIDATION_SOURCE_BUDGET_CHARS=48000   # lowering it makes the validator judge a partial view
# SUMMARY_COVERAGE_TARGET=0.70
# SUMMARY_MAX_LLM_CALLS=500
# SUMMARY_ON_INGEST=true              # build the collection summary at the end of an ingest


# =============================================================================
# 17. Storage
# =============================================================================
# In Docker these are pinned by compose to volume paths, because the
# $HOME-derived defaults are unwritable in the hardened container.
# DATA_PATH=~/docint/data
# QDRANT_SRC_DIR=~/docint/qdrant_sources
# RESULTS_PATH=~/docint/results
# EXTRACT_DIR=~/docint/extracts     # rendered collection extracts
#
# Extract bundles (see docs/extracts.md).
# EXTRACT_RETENTION_DAYS=7
# EXTRACT_MAX_PER_COLLECTION=5
# EXTRACT_PDF_MAX_UNITS=200         # 0 disables the combined PDF
# EXTRACT_PDF_MAX_FIGURES=400
# EXTRACT_SYNC_MAX_UNITS=50         # above this a per-source download queues a job
# DOCINT_EXTRACT_CONCURRENCY=1
#
# Vector quantization. `turbo` trades a little recall for much less RAM.
# QDRANT_QUANTIZATION=turbo           # turbo | none
# QDRANT_TURBOQUANT_BITS=bits4        # bits4 | bits2 | bits1_5 | bits1


# =============================================================================
# 18. Frontend limits
# =============================================================================
# DOCINT_CLIENT_MAX_BODY_SIZE is read by BOTH the backend (advertised via
# GET /config so the SPA sizes upload batches) and the frontend nginx image
# (which enforces it). The two must stay in sync.
# DOCINT_CLIENT_MAX_BODY_SIZE=1g
# FRONTEND_COLLECTION_TIMEOUT=120
# Most findings one "Add all" may put in a report. Bound into the request model
# at import (restart to change) and advertised via GET /config, so the SPA
# refuses an oversize section against the number the API enforces.
# REPORT_BATCH_MAX_ITEMS=2000


# =============================================================================
# 19. Docker and build only — never read by the Python backend
# =============================================================================
# DOCINT_HOST_PORT=8080               # host port for the SPA; docker/compose.override.yaml (make up-dev)
# DOCINT_API_MAX_BODY_SIZE=64m        # nginx request-body cap on the JSON API locations (report batch add)
# EXTRA_NO_PROXY=                     # appended to NO_PROXY; must start with a comma
# INFERENCE_NET=inference-net         # name of the external inference network
# PRELOAD_MODELS=false                # true runs `load-models` in the container CMD before uvicorn
# TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM=false        # read by the vendored tokenizers/transformers, not by docint
